"""
Canela on macOS: one window over one Markdown file, rendered while it is
typed (spec v0 B1.1, B1.2), on the core of Wolly (Wolly.Editor,
Wolly.EditorView, Wolly.Platform).

The file named on the command line is opened, or a new one made under that
name when it does not exist; the file is plain Markdown (B1.3) and is
written only by Command+S and when the window closes with changes, each time
as a whole, atomically.  Keys: typing and the input method, Return,
Shift+Return, Backspace, Delete, the arrows (with Shift a selection), Home
and End, Page Up and Down; Command+Z undo, Command+Shift+Z redo, Command+S
save, Command+1 to 6 a heading, Command+0 a paragraph, Command+A all,
Command+C, X and V the clipboard, Command+W and Q close.  A click places the
cursor or ticks a task.

Limits: one file a window; no menu, no file dialog, no search; the fonts
are Arial and Menlo of macOS, without a fallback for other scripts.

    canela notes.md
"""
module Canela.App is
    """
    Opens the window over the file named by the first argument and runs
    until it closes; the exit status is 1 when the last save failed.
    No contract: the entry of the programme.
    """
    function main(root: RootCapability): ExitCode;
end module.
